                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "its simply not very good.\n\nIt's a puzzle game, but the puzzles exclusively consist of finding a path through a bunch of excessively long corridors, with a bunch of pointless death obstacles, where its only any kind of mystery where you're going because it has an awful perspective. Its only solvable via trial and error.\n\nThe idea for the story is mildly interesting, an experiment where someone becomes able to age at will, but the execution is terrible and it ends up being incredibly generic. There's a guy who talks a lot at you without saying anything helpful, or really plot relevant, which you are forced to repeat every time you die. The dialogue has a lot of very clunky wording, and tries really hard to be mysterious only to fall very flat. \n\nThe art style would probably work absolutely fine for a 2D game but as an isometric 3D game, especially combined with the pointlessly long corridors and awkward camera angle, just doesn't hit.",
